From 8b8d5289ec1ea9c56d4334c16a8e49dee06dfc21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 14:43:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/53] kaiair: PktR signal (gain) map, feeds GRK
 exclusion-region sizing (Phase 1, T1.3)

The "who-hears-whom" gain map GRK runs on. Path gains G(tx,rx) = rx_reference_power
- tx_power (dB), EWMA-smoothed, keyed per ordered (tx,rx) pair; per-node tx power +
activity held alongside. Gains come from reference signals (RSRP + PHR in-cell,
neighbour SSB-RSRP cross-cell via reciprocity), never the aggregate SINR.

- lib/scheduler/kaiair/pktr_signal_map.h: update_gain(), set_node(), gain_db(),
  candidates_for(rx, intended) -> grk_interferer rows ready for
  pktr_grk::size_exclusion_region.
- pktr_signal_map_test.cpp: 6 tests incl. a 2-cell end-to-end (UE_B interfering at
  gNB_A over budget -> excluded, K = G_TR - G_CR). All 6 PktR suites pass.

A fixed dBFS<->dBm RX offset cancels in the GRK gain ratio K, so the ER is correct
with relative gains. Not yet wired into the metrics view (Step 3 / T3.4).
